<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116253" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠν-ητός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ός</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Hel.</u>
			816
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bought,</i> of slaves, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμὲ δ᾽ ὠνητὴ τέκε μήτηρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.202
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοῦλος οὐκ ὠνητὸς ἀλλ᾽ οἴκοι τραφείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					1123
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				365
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				841d
			</span></i>, etc.; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίσθιος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				16
			</span></i>: but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠνητὴ δύναμις</span> a
				<i>mercenary</i> force, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκεία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.121
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠν. σῖτος,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δωρητός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cor.</u>
				16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be bought, that may be bought,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλπίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					816
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					978
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλεῖαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					544d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1273a36
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>APl.</u>
					4.80
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>): c. gen. pretii, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόξα χρημάτων οὐκ
				ὠνητή</span> not <i>to be bought for</i> money, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				2.32
			</span></i>: but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλπὶς χρήμασιν ὠνητή</span>
			<i>with</i> money, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.40
			</span></i>.</div>
